<%# Reviewer decision reason form (civora-org/civora-platform#90), the
    return/reject transition control on the admin index rows: a collapsed
    <details> keeps the row compact (the redaction-card precedent) and
    opens onto a small plain form_with — textarea + submit, no JS beyond
    the Rails UJS confirm carried over from the bare buttons it replaces.
    Plain tag helpers on purpose (the import_crz form precedent): this is
    a url-based POST form with no model object behind it — the Decidim
    FormBuilder's validation machinery reads the (absent) form object, and
    a builder label next to a field helper is the repo's double-label
    seam. The textarea's NAME stays the server-side contract (`reason`,
    passed through to TransitionContract, the single authority on the
    judgment vocabulary) while the id is derived per record and event, so
    several decision rows can share one page without colliding labels —
    the same seam as the redaction checkbox. The required attribute and
    the maxlength cap are UX aids, never the gate: the command re-checks
    both server-side, fail-closed. Locals:
      contract - the record under review
      event    - the judgment event (:return or :reject); the summary and
                 the submit reuse the established transition.<event> label
                 vocabulary — never a second one. %>
<% field_id = "review_reason_#{contract.id}_#{event}" %>
<details class="review-decision">
  <summary><%= t("decidim.contracts_sk.admin.contracts.transition.#{event}") %></summary>
  <div class="card-section">
    <%= form_with url: public_send(:"#{event}_admin_contract_path", contract), method: :post, local: true do %>
      <div class="row column">
        <%= label_tag field_id, t("decidim.contracts_sk.admin.contracts.transition.review_reason.label") %>
        <%= text_area_tag :reason, nil, id: field_id,
                                        placeholder: t("decidim.contracts_sk.admin.contracts.transition.review_reason.placeholder"),
                                        maxlength: Decidim::ContractsSk::Admin::TransitionContract::MAX_REASON_LENGTH,
                                        required: true %>
      </div>
      <%= submit_tag t("decidim.contracts_sk.admin.contracts.transition.#{event}"),
                     class: "button button__sm button__secondary",
                     data: { confirm: t("decidim.contracts_sk.admin.contracts.transition.confirm.#{event}") } %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</details>
